WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.070
Blue's Clues star Steve Burns was pretty much
every late '90s kid's pretend best friend

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:09.420
as he took them on colorful new mysteries
around the house and outside with his trusty pooch pal.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.940
The show, which centered on Steve and his
dog Blue making an interactive adventure of

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:18.710
even the simplest things like checking the
mail, ranked right up there with popular contemporaries

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.440
like Barney, the Teletubbies, and Winnie the
Pooh.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:25.960
So, when Steve suddenly disappeared from the
hit program and was replaced at the height

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:31.199
of its popularity, the rumor mill went haywire,
even going so far as to declare the young

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:35.040
show host had died to explain his unexpected
departure.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.430
Luckily, Steve is still alive and well … even
though his former fans might not be able to

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:40.700
spot him walking around town.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.460
"I am completely unrecognizable now."

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:47.320
What he's been up to since taking his leave
of the small screen might just surprise you.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:50.920
Here's what's become of former Blue's Clues
star Steve Burns.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.500
Exit signs

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.660
The obvious first question most people have
about what happened to Steve Burns is

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:00.160
"Why did the guy leave the show right in the middle
of its prime?"

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:06.360
No, he didn't have some other lucrative offer
luring him away, nor did he fall into a pit of depression.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:11.820
But he did start to lose his hair and watched
some behind-the-scenes creatives take their leave, too.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.860
So for him, it was just time to go when he
did.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.180
There were also a few practical considerations
at play.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:20.100
"It was crazy.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:27.100
It was awesome, but it was not exactly the
kind of thing that would get me a date."

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.659
One of the other factors that had Steve questioning
his reality while he was such a central kid's

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:37.310
show icon is whether the wacky messages he
was delivering to so many millions of little

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:39.560
ones were actually worthy of their attention.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:42.220
"'You can do anything that you want to do.'

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:45.060
But I couldn't help thinking, you know, is
that true?"

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:46.540
Still alive

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:51.380
Blue's Clues might've come along during the
advent of the internet age, but pop culture

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:53.700
urban legends still loomed large at the time.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:58.940
Somehow, rumors spread like wildfire that
Steve died of a drug overdose or a grisly

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:04.300
car wreck in between Seasons 4 and 5, even
though in the last episode of Season 4, Steve

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:08.680
introduced his own replacement — Steve's
brother Joe, played by Donovan Patton for

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.060
the final two seasons of the show.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:14.600
In 2017, he spoke to Tech Insider about the
persistent death hoax:

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:23.540
"To be rumored to be dead for 15 years starts
to feel disturbingly like a cultural preference."

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:29.460
Nowadays, Burns makes light of the rumors
with the Twitter handle @SteveBurnsAlive — to

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:31.820
both have fun with the misunderstanding and
clear it up.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:33.880
Making art

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:39.300
Although Burns hasn't nearly re-claimed the
same level of fame that he had on Blue's Clues,

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.960
he hasn't shelved his stack of old headshots
entirely just yet.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:47.860
He appeared on-stage for The Moth to wax poetic
with a true-life telling of his time as a

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:53.960
children's TV show star and also starred in
The Flaming Lips' weird space-centric holiday video.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:58.160
He's also been seen starring on webisodes
of small YouTube shows like The Professionals

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:03.550
and even appearing alongside another blue
storytelling pal for Bizarro Studio's Herman's

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.280
Scary Stories series.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:10.420
Of course, those cameos alone probably aren't
enough to pay the bills, and his Blue's Clues

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:12.180
residuals can't last forever …

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.980
"I wanted to know how you've been doing with
my money.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:16.740
Well?"

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:18.700
"Broke!"

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:23.380
So, Burns has steadily been moving forward
on that music career he's been working on

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:24.600
for so long all the while.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:31.940
"I'm just a boring example of everybody else."

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:36.060
He fulfilled his own childhood dream by releasing
his own record and, when his solo act wasn't

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:41.000
hacking it, he linked up with The Flaming
Lips alum Steven Drozd to begin working on an album.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:46.000
Thanks to the popularity of Blue's Clues with
a producer's kid, Steve was well known before

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.100
he ever made his big pitch.

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:50.820
Hey, it's not like he hadn't shown off his
skills on the show already.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:55.300
The two have since formed a project called
Steven Steven and put together a trippy kids'

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:58.720
album titled Foreverywhere, which drops in
February, 2017.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:00.220
Free time

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:05.320
Although his music making and random acting
jobs are fun enough, Steve Burns also has

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:09.930
enough time to bring his fans in on some of
his other obsessions, like taking pictures

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:15.790
of every Walmart sign he sees and, yes, even
the occasional bit of nostalgia and puns about

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:18.000
his former life as Steve of Blue's Clues.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:22.820
Although the show is now far in the past for
Steve Burns, he does keep a few reminders

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.740
lying around the house for old time's sake.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:26.740
"The chair sits in my study…

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:28.640
I love it.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.040
I have the original notebook.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.500
I have the first three clues, which is cool."

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:34.560
Thanks for watching!

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:37.100
